# The music analysis Worker's runtime on Debian 13 (CPython 3.13, x86_64):
# allin1 with harmonix-all (docs/architecture/montage-music.md). The runtime's
# packages and hashes are in requirements.txt, which
#   scripts/build-videocut-music-runtime.sh --lock
# resolves from this file with uv. NATTEN and madmom have no wheels for this
# Python: sources.json pins their sources, which the build turns into wheels.
#
# allin1 and the Demucs it separates the stems with; allin1 asks for NATTEN
# on macOS alone, and for madmom not at all.
allin1==1.1.0
demucs==4.1.0
# PyTorch for the processor alone, from PyTorch's own index: the build
# compiles NATTEN against this version.
torch==2.6.0+cpu
# allin1 reads its checkpoints' configuration with OmegaConf 2; without these
# bounds the resolver falls back to Hydra 0.11, whose antlr4 runtime it would
# otherwise build from source (it is pure Python: --no-binary allows it).
hydra-core>=1.3
omegaconf>=2.3
# madmom's own requirements (its setup.py).
scipy
mido
# What NATTEN and madmom are built with.
cython
setuptools
wheel
packaging
